---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import Showcase from "../../../components/Showcase.astro";
import { TagDemo } from "../../../components/react-demos/tag";

const install = `pnpm add @skryensya/core @skryensya/react`;

const html = `<div class="sk-inline">
  <span class="sk-tag">
    <span class="sk-tag__label">design</span>
  </span>
  <span class="sk-tag" data-tone="accent">
    <span class="sk-tag__label">tokens</span>
  </span>
  <span class="sk-tag" data-tone="success">
    <span class="sk-tag__label">activo</span>
  </span>
  <span class="sk-tag" data-tone="warning">
    <span class="sk-tag__label">beta</span>
  </span>
  <span class="sk-tag" data-tone="danger">
    <span class="sk-tag__label">deprecado</span>
  </span>
  <span class="sk-tag" data-tone="accent">
    <span class="sk-tag__label">react</span>
    <button
      class="sk-button sk-interactive sk-tag__remove"
      type="button"
      data-variant="ghost"
      data-size="sm"
      data-icon-only
      aria-label="Quitar react"
    >
      <span data-sk-icon="close"></span>
    </button>
  </span>
  <span class="sk-tag">
    <span class="sk-tag__label">frontend</span>
    <button
      class="sk-button sk-interactive sk-tag__remove"
      type="button"
      data-variant="ghost"
      data-size="sm"
      data-icon-only
      aria-label="Quitar frontend"
    >
      <span data-sk-icon="close"></span>
    </button>
  </span>
</div>`;

const react = `import { Tag } from "@skryensya/react/tag";

function Example() {
  return (
    <div className="sk-inline">
      <Tag>design</Tag>
      <Tag tone="accent">tokens</Tag>
      <Tag tone="success">activo</Tag>
      <Tag tone="warning">beta</Tag>
      <Tag tone="danger">deprecado</Tag>
      <Tag
        tone="accent"
        onRemove={SomeFunction}
        removeLabel="Quitar react"
      >
        react
      </Tag>
      <Tag onRemove={SomeFunction} removeLabel="Quitar frontend">
        frontend
      </Tag>
    </div>
  );
}`;
---

<Base title="Tag" description="Tag: optionally removable keyword chip, with tones and React component.">
  <h1>Tag</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Tag classifies content that the user can act on: filters, facets, chips. Where <a href="/en/components/badge">Badge</a> is a read-only status tag, Tag is more square (control radius, not pill) to be read as actionable, and may carry a remove button.
  </p>

  <Showcase html={html} react={react} label="Tag">
    <Fragment slot="react">
      <TagDemo client:load />
    </Fragment>
  </Showcase>
  <p>
    When removable, the tag and the remove button are two different targets: the control's accessible name names the tag it removes.
  </p>

  <h2>The X is a Button, not a drawing of one</h2>
  <p>
    The remove control is an actual <a href="/en/components/button">Button</a> — <code>sk-button sk-interactive</code> with <code>data-size="sm"</code>, <code>data-icon-only</code>, and <code>data-variant="ghost"</code> — and <code>sk-tag__remove</code> is just the modifier that shrinks it to the height of the capsule. Tag does not send its own interaction.
  </p>
  <p>
    What you gain is what you no longer have to maintain here: the hover and the press come from the <a href="/en/state-layer">state layer</a>, the focus ring is the same as all the controls, and the touch area reaches <strong>44px</strong> by the <code>:: after</code> of the button even though the face paints 20px. Before they were 20px for face and 20px for useful white.
  </p>
  <p>
    The color is still <code>currentColor</code>, so each shade brings its X in its own color without a per-tone rule.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={install} label="terminal" />

  <h2>React</h2>
  <p>The code is in the <strong>React</strong> tab of the preview. <code>onRemove</code> is optional.</p>
</Base>
